cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the article and the software via these metadata."
type: software
title: "Mining-ADAS-ACW: Reference implementation of classification-guided Adaptive Clockwork multitask perception for open-pit mining"
abstract: >-
  Official source code for a video-based multitask scene-perception pipeline
  for open-pit mining ADAS that combines drivable-area semantic segmentation
  and steering-direction classification within a single BiSeNetV1 backbone.
  Introduces Adaptive Clockwork (A-CW), a classification-guided inference
  policy that updates the slow Context Path only on keyframes whose cadence is
  decided online by a learned scheduler. Ships clean baselines for
  Frame-by-Frame, Fixed Clockwork, Deep Feature Flow and Low-Latency Method
  on the same backbone, plus end-to-end FPS benchmarks and a simulated
  1080x720 HMI rendering module.
